30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance. Also, whole-building lets are risky if people cancel last minute.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Inland centers sound like a nightmare for sleep—eight to a room is unacceptable for athletes. Campus might be better, but is it feasible?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Public bookings are a huge amount of paperwork and a lottery. Also, cooking for ourselves on campus takes way too much time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Transport is a massive drain on the budget. Public beds are cheap, but the travel to get there might cancel out the savings.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"If we want the year-groups to mix, we have to stay together in one place. Also, some people just stop coming if it's too hard.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we stay together, we risk the non-refundable deposit issue I found. We need a balance of cohesion and financial safety.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Minato, if the campus canteen is closed and the hall is crowded, ""Campus Intensive"" sounds like a logistical disaster for recovery.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minato,,I'm worried about the organizers. A nine-page application for a public center sounds like it would take forever to finish.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, the budget is already tight. We can't afford a destination that spikes transport costs or leaves us with unpaid gaps.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, but if we stay on campus, we don't have that transport cost. The problem is we won't bond if we just go home.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Campus is the safest for the budget, but @Shion mentioned the hall might be crowded. We should consider the options carefully.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shion,,"I've seen the train times; a third of us can't even make it to campus by 9 AM without a hotel. Campus isn't ""free.""","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minato,,I think we should avoid the public centers. The lottery and the paperwork seem too stressful for the staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we go to a lodge, we avoid the lottery and the cooking, but the transport and the fixed headcount are risks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Takumi,,A lodge where we all stay in one building is the only way to fix the club's atmosphere. We need that shared time.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We have to weigh the social benefit against the financial risk of a non-refundable deposit and high transport costs.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'm leaning away from the Mountain Centre. Eight people to a room is a recipe for a failed training camp.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minato,,I agree. Let's find something that doesn't require a nine-page form or two hours of cooking a day.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I can't support any option where the final cost is unpredictable. We need a fixed, manageable expense.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Let's prioritize the club's future. If people are quitting because they don't feel connected, the budget doesn't matter.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
